<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.2">
  <DUT Name="ST_Shaker" Id="{91397fcc-47b0-4fa6-90e4-4877149b614d}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Purpose : Interface structure of one shaker channel of an M3 selector
              (sample-delivery). It groups the four signals of the channel: the
              field power output, the interlock permissive, the local switch
              input and the EPICS on/off command.

    Usage   : Instantiated four times per selector as stShaker01..stShaker04 in
              FB_SelectorM3 and published as Shaker:01..Shaker:04 of the
              selector instance (e.g. XCS:SDS:SEL:A..D:Shaker:01..04 in the
              sds-m101 deployment; the P prefix follows the deployment).
              FB_SelectorM3 services each channel with a plain copy every scan,
                  stShakerNN.q_xPwrDO := stShakerNN.i_xEpics;
              so the EPICS command reaches the field with no interlock gating,
              no local-switch gating and no delay. xIlk and i_xSwitch are read
              by no logic in this library, so populating them here does not
              inhibit the output.

    Objectives: - one named interface per shaker, shared by the deployment GVL,
                  the selector FB and the generated EPICS records;
                - keep command (i_xEpics), field output (q_xPwrDO), interlock
                  (xIlk) and local switch (i_xSwitch) apart, so that the
                  interlock and EPICS command paths cannot be cross-wired
                  without being noticed.

    Polarity: all four members are TRUE-active; nothing in this type is
              inverted. q_xPwrDO TRUE energizes the digital output. xIlk is the
              conditioned permissive - TRUE = interlocks satisfied, FALSE (or an
              open/broken fail-safe contact) not permitted - so whoever writes
              xIlk must have applied the normally-closed inversion already; this
              structure does not do it. i_xSwitch and i_xEpics TRUE are "shaker
              on" requests.

    Units   : none - all four members are BOOL. q_xPwrDO is a raw %Q* terminal
              bit (24 V on the EP2338-1001 digital output channel it is linked
              to; channels 9..12 carry shakers 1..4 of that selector). The other
              three are software booleans, published to EPICS by the pytmc
              pragmas on the members.

    History : 2023-05-19 J. Zamudio - type added with the initial commit
              (746deac), no member documented.
              2025-05-29 J. Zamudio - moved to Library/DUTs in the project
              restructure (9b2fb2c), contents unchanged.
              2026-11-27 Scirix Agent - added this header and one comment per
              member (audit finding 442); no member, type or pragma changed.
*)
TYPE ST_Shaker :
STRUCT

// Power output of the shaker. Raw %Q* terminal bit, TRUE = output energized (24 V
// on the linked EP2338-1001 channel), FALSE = de-energized. Boolean, no unit.
// Driven every scan by FB_SelectorM3 from i_xEpics; the deployment GVL links
// shakers 1..4 to channels 9..12 of that selector's "M3 Selector x Digital IO".
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: PowerOn
    io: i
 '}
q_xPwrDO AT %Q*	:	BOOL;

// External interlock permissive of the shaker. TRUE = interlocks satisfied and
// the shaker may run, FALSE = not permitted. Fail-safe normally closed: the raw
// field contact is inverted by the caller, this structure inverts nothing.
// Boolean, no unit. Read by no logic today - FB_SelectorM3 does not gate
// q_xPwrDO with it - so the EPICS readback (pv Ilk) stays FALSE and does not
// actually inhibit the output.
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: Ilk
    io: i
 '}
xIlk		:	BOOL;


// Local field switch of the shaker. TRUE = switch in the on position, FALSE =
// off. Boolean, no unit. Software input only: it carries no pytmc pragma (so it
// is not published to EPICS) and no logic in this library reads it.
i_xSwitch	:	BOOL;

// EPICS on/off command for the shaker. TRUE = operator requests the shaker on,
// FALSE = off. Boolean, no unit. The only member EPICS writes (pv Ctrl);
// FB_SelectorM3 copies it unchanged into q_xPwrDO, so neither xIlk nor
// i_xSwitch gates this path.
{attribute 'pytmc' := '
    pv: Ctrl
    io: o
 '}
i_xEpics	:	BOOL;

END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>